This is the standard Exercism grep exercise. Note that the tests mock `grep.open` — meaning my implementation needs to call `open` (the built-in) directly inside grep.py, and it will be patched via `mock.patch("grep.open", create=True)`. So I should use plain `open(fname)` inside the function.

Implementing the standard solution:

```python
def grep(pattern, flags, files):
    flags = set(flags.split())
    show_line_numbers = "-n" in flags
    show_file_names = "-l" in flags
    ignore_case = "-i" in flags
    invert = "-v" in flags
    whole_line = "-x" in flags

    output = []
    for filename in files:
        with open(filename) as f:
            lines = f.readlines()

        if ignore_case:
            pattern = pattern.lower()

        for line_number, line in enumerate(lines, start=1):
            text = line.rstrip("\n")
            if ignore_case:
                haystack = text.lower()
            else:
                haystack = text
            matched = (haystack == pattern) if whole_line else (pattern in haystack)
            if matched != invert:
                if show_file_names:
                    if not any(out.startswith(filename + ":") for out in output):
                        output.append(filename + "\n")
                else:
                    prefix = ""
                    if len(files) > 1:
                        prefix += filename + ":"
                    if show_line_numbers:
                        prefix += str(line_number) + ":"
                    output.append(prefix + text + "\n")
    return "".join(output)
```

